{
  "_notes": {
    "normalization": "All ground-truth values are stored canonical: money as plain number string with 2 decimals and no $ or commas (e.g. 84210.55); dates as YYYY-MM-DD; EIN as NN-NNNNNNN; SSN/TIN last4 as 4 digits; names UPPERCASE with single spaces; codes UPPERCASE; checkboxes as true/false; tax_year as 4-digit string. score.py applies the same normalization to model output before exact-match.",
    "redaction": "Synthetic identities only. SSNs are printed on the documents as XXX-XX-1234 (last 4 visible), which matches how redacted client copies look. EINs are synthetic.",
    "scoring": "field-level exact match after normalization. A missing field counts as wrong. Per-doc accuracy = correct/total fields; area accuracy = micro-average over all fields in all docs."
  },
